        "id": 137108,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-12T16:24:54.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Move is a limited action, so i'm pretty sure Bots can only only use it once as well.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I don't actually believe this is the case Ronway. To use move as one of your actions is limited, yes, but since moving her bots is a fuction of the Unlimited Go Bots! action, I think you may choose any of those actions multiple times.</p>\n<p>I believe this holds true for Proletariats Overwhelm, where you may \"Overwhelm\" an any of your actions, even if it is one you have already used (Like Clone for example).</p>\n<p>Paul or Luther, please let me know if I am off track here. I'm not 100% sure on this.</p>",
