        "id": 137110,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-12T17:09:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think Ronway's right, but that's my interpretation - it'll be good to get an official answer on this one.</p><p>Unity can use Go Bots to allow a bot to use an action. By definition, the common actions (Move, et al) are limited, so the bot can't do one of those more than once.&nbsp;</p><p>What is sometimes missed is that Swift Bot can use it's attack action which allows it to move and then execute an attack, which can look like it just moved, again. That might be part of what folks are seeing.</p>",
